{"RunId":"2c9d839f-c609-4830-81b2-3263f312c85a","Seq":28,"Kind":"NodeCompleted","Synthetic":true,"TimestampUtc":"2026-04-25T01:11:55.0795221Z","NodeId":"n_ym05bcg","NodeName":null,"Payload":{"nodeInstanceId":"2b266f96-eb47-487a-950b-e5c723a75dcc","duration":"PT1M35.4739876S","inputData":{"triggerType":"WebHook","triggerTime":"2026-04-25T01:10:19.5800626Z","webHookMethod":"POST","webHookRoute":"/webhook/investigate-icm","bodyJsonSchema":"{\n   \u0022type\u0022: \u0022object\u0022,\n   \u0022required\u0022: [\u0022incidentId\u0022, \u0022serviceName\u0022, \u0022teamName\u0022, \u0022timestamp\u0022],\n   \u0022properties\u0022: {\n     \u0022incidentId\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022integer\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022int64\u0022 },\n     \u0022serviceName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022teamName\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022 },\n     \u0022timestamp\u0022: { \u0022type\u0022: \u0022string\u0022, \u0022format\u0022: \u0022date-time\u0022 }\n   }\n }","messageType":"json","body.timestamp":"2026-04-25T01:10:14.008Z","body.incidentId":783872773,"body.serviceName":"","body.teamName":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 783872773,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022teamName\u0022: \u0022\u0022,\n  \u0022timestamp\u0022: \u00222026-04-25T01:10:14.008Z\u0022\n}"},"outputData":{"mode":"skill","backend":"copilot","model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","agentName":"open-icm","agentSummary":"","result":"The discussion is mostly rendered UI components with base64 images \u2014 the actual discussion thread content is minimal. Based on what was successfully extracted, here\u0027s my analysis:\n\n---\n\n## ICM Incident 783872773 \u2014 Investigation Summary\n\n### Incident Details\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Incident ID** | 783872773 |\n| **Status** | Active |\n| **Severity** | Sev 3 |\n| **Service** | **Azure Stack HCI** |\n| **Owning Team** | **Arc Managed VMs** |\n| **Owner** | Michael Duppr\u00E9 (mduppre) |\n| **Region** | USGovVirginia |\n| **Cluster** | \u0060/subscriptions/f726effd.../resourceGroups/choliv-test-rg/providers/microsoft.azurestackhci/clusters/ceo-clu001\u0060 |\n\n---\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe customer cannot delete an orphaned network interface (\u0060arcvm001-NIC\u0060) left behind after VM \u0060arcvm001\u0060 was deleted from the portal. The deletion request is being **blocked by the admission webhook** (\u0060createupdatevalidationwebhook.infrastructure.azstackhci.microsoft.com\u0060) with:\n\n\u003E *\u0022The following IP Pool ranges you entered are already in use: [10.10.35.52, 10.10.35.61] by ceo-clu001-InfraLNET. Please choose different ranges to avoid conflicts.\u0022*\n\n---\n\n### Root Cause / Contributing Factors\n\n1. **Post-upgrade LNET overlap**: After upgrading from Azure Local **2512 \u2192 2601**, an infrastructure LNET (\u0060ceo-clu001-Infra-LNET\u0060) was automatically created with an IP range overlapping the pre-existing \u0060LNET1-Static\u0060.\n\n2. **Validation webhook fires on DELETE**: The admission webhook is incorrectly triggering IP pool conflict validation during a **NIC deletion** operation. A delete should not require IP range uniqueness checks \u2014 this is a webhook logic bug.\n\n3. **Orphaned resource state**: The NIC became orphaned (parent VM deleted) but the resource still exists in the control plane, unable to be GC\u0027d due to the erroneous validation block.\n\n---\n\n### Impact\n- **Low blast radius**: Internal test stamp only (\u0060choliv-test-rg\u0060), no customer workloads affected.\n- **Blocked**: Resource cleanup is stalled; customer cannot reprovision the LNET or create new VMs using those IPs.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Next Steps\n\n1. **Immediate mitigation**: Investigate if the orphaned NIC can be force-deleted by bypassing the webhook (e.g., directly via ARM or by temporarily disabling the webhook on the cluster). The owning team (Arc Managed VMs) should check if a \u0060kubectl delete\u0060 on the underlying CRD resolves the stale resource.\n\n2. **Root cause fix**: The validation webhook should **not** apply IP pool conflict checks on DELETE operations for NICs. A code fix should be filed to scope the validation to create/update only.\n\n3. **Post-upgrade LNET overlap**: Investigate why the 2601 upgrade created an infra LNET with overlapping IPs \u2014 the upgrade logic should validate against existing LNETs before auto-provisioning infra networking resources.\n\n4. **Escalation path**: Since this is USGovVirginia and logs cannot be accessed directly, coordinate with the Arc Managed VMs on-call to retrieve cluster-side logs from the webhook controller.\n\n---\n\n[OUTPUT:incidentFolder] E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\n[OUTPUT:summary.md] 1 KB \u2014 orphaned NIC deletion blocked by validation webhook after 2512\u21922601 upgrade\n[OUTPUT:discussion.md] 380 KB (mostly rendered UI, minimal discussion text captured)\n[OUTPUT:rca.md] 3 KB \u2014 IP range overlap between infra LNET and existing LNET after upgrade\n[OUTPUT:metadata.md] 1 KB \u2014 Service: Azure Stack HCI, Team: Arc Managed VMs, Owner: mduppre\n[OUTPUT:ai_summary.md] (not present)","ai.success":true,"ai.model":"claude-sonnet-4.6","ai.durationMs":85326,"ai.inputTokens":250721,"ai.outputTokens":2550,"incidentFolder":"E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773","summary.md":"1 KB \u2014 orphaned NIC deletion blocked by validation webhook after 2512\u21922601 upgrade","discussion.md":"380 KB (mostly rendered UI, minimal discussion text captured)","rca.md":"3 KB \u2014 IP range overlap between infra LNET and existing LNET after upgrade","metadata.md":"1 KB \u2014 Service: Azure Stack HCI, Team: Arc Managed VMs, Owner: mduppre","ai_summary.md":"(not present)"},"globalVariables":{"maxQueryScore":0,"body.timestamp":"2026-04-25T01:10:14.008Z","codeIssueFile":"","__webhookBody":"{\n  \u0022incidentId\u0022: 783872773,\n  \u0022serviceName\u0022: \u00